  "finalText": "I've fixed the issue the verifier found, and it was correct.\n\n**What was wrong:** T-1999 is an automated alert: payments pipelines have been failing more than half the time since Saturday night. That's the same problem as T-2003 and T-2012, which I had already merged. I'd left T-1999 open on its own, even though it carried an earlier committed deadline (23 March, 10:30 UTC) than the 12:10 I gave T-2003. The handbook says the merged ticket keeps the earliest deadline in the set.\n\n**What I changed:**\n- **Merged T-1999 into T-2003.** T-2003 is still the main ticket because it was reported first (21 March, 22:30). No other tickets linked to T-1999, so there were no references to move.\n- **Moved T-2003's deadline to 23 March, 10:30 UTC** (it was 12:10). This is an existing commitment, so no deadline moved earlier than what a requester had already been promised.\n- **Left T-2003's other settings as they were:** sev2, department-wide impact, assigned to E-101 Dana Whitfield. She's on call for the platform rotation from 08:00 to 20:00 today, which covers 10:30, and she has no leave recorded.\n- **Added a comment on T-2003** recording the merge and the new deadline.\n\nI didn't touch anything else.",
